  "answer_text": "**wakehealth.edu** is the official website for **Atrium Health Wake Forest Baptist** (historically known as Wake Forest Baptist Health). \n\nBased in Winston-Salem, North Carolina, it is a prominent academic medical center and health system integrated with the **Wake Forest University School of Medicine** and is a part of the larger **Advocate Health** network.\n\nBelow is an overview of what you can find and do on the website:\n\n### 1. Patient Portal (MyAtriumHealth)\n* **The Transition:** If you previously used the **myWakeHealth** patient portal, the system has transitioned to **MyAtriumHealth** (powered by Epic MyChart). \n* **Accessing Your Account:** You can log in using your existing myWakeHealth username and password. \n* **Features:** Through the portal, you can message your care team, view test results, manage prescriptions, schedule appointments, conduct video visits, and pay bills.\n\n### 2. Clinical Services & Finding Care\n* **Find a Doctor:** Search the directory for primary care doctors, pediatricians, and specialists operating across western North Carolina.\n* **Hospitals and Locations:** Find directions, hours, and contact information for the main **Atrium Health Wake Forest Baptist Medical Center**, **Brenner Children's Hospital**, and regional community hospitals (such as those in Alleghany, Davie, Lexington, and Wilkes counties).\n* **Specialty Centers:** Access information on major specialty care programs, including the NCI-designated Comprehensive Cancer Center, Heart and Vascular services, and Level I Trauma Centers.\n\n### 3. Acadics, Research, & Education\n* **Wake Forest University School of Medicine:** The website provides portals for medical students, residents, fellows, and researchers.\n* **Clinical Trials:** Patients and doctors can search for ongoing clinical trials and medical research being conducted in Winston-Salem and the surrounding Innovation Quarter.\n\n### 4. For Employees & Medical Staff\n* The site features dedicated quick links for employees, allowing staff to access internal networks, medical library databases, and employee benefits portals using their medical center credentials.",
